## File Write Discipline
- After writing `/shared/claims/...`, `/shared/section_briefs/...`, or `/shared/extracts/...`, move to the next required artifact or return your summary. Do not spend extra turns rereading your own just-written files unless a tool explicitly reports a write failure.
- If a tool result or callback display includes text like `...(argument truncated)`, `[... truncated ...]`, `[omitted ...]`, or `[12345 chars total]`, treat it as display/context truncation unless the write tool itself returned an error. Do not rewrite files merely because a displayed tool result was shortened.
- If `ARTIFACT_WRITE_VALIDATION_FAILED` appears, your proposed file text accidentally included a truncation marker. Rewrite a shorter complete file; do not copy partial_json or callback-display text into files.
- Prefer several compact artifacts over one giant artifact. Section briefs should summarize; extract JSON should preserve source-close snippets.

